{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning everyone. I'm Maj. Rowan, Maintenance Control Officer. We need to get moving on the quarter-end property reconciliation for the items currently tagged unserviceable — battery packs, rugged tablets, power converters, and electronic test cables. Before I can sign off on disposition orders, I need current technical status and disposition recommendations confirmed with the responsible sections. Let's start by hearing from each section on where these items stand and what disposition category they recommend: quarantine, reissue, repair, or calibration return."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "Sir, the battery shop confirmed this morning that the six unserviceable battery packs have swollen casings covered by a manufacturer safety bulletin. They must be quarantined rather than repaired. We have property-office pickup scheduled for Wednesday at 1000. I should note that the inspection sheet is still in the shop binder and has not been entered in the maintenance control log yet."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "Ma'am, IT support has completed certified data erasure on all eight rugged tablets and found them serviceable for the training cell. They need to be reissued to the training cell with an asset transfer scheduled for Friday at 0900. The erasure certificates are filed in the IT ticket system, but I should note they are not currently attached to the reconciliation packet."}
```

